READ THIS FIRST

This is a source-available license, not an open-source one. The code is public so
you can read it, learn from it and try it. Money is what changes the rules.

Free, no permission needed
  - personal study, experiments, hobby and portfolio projects;
  - coursework, teaching, and academic research;
  - reading the code, cloning it, running it on your own machine;
  - changing it for any of the above, as long as what you distribute stays
    noncommercial.

Needs a paid commercial license, in writing, before you start
  - using this software, or code copied from it, in a product or service a company
    sells, or in tooling a company runs its business on;
  - hosting it for other people: a SaaS, a demo a company pays for, an internal
    assistant at work;
  - paid client work, consulting deliverables, or anything shipped under a
    company's name;
  - training another model on it, or bundling it into something commercial.

To buy one, mail kumar.harshzzz04@gmail.com with the company, what you intend to do
with the software, and roughly how many people or machines would run it. A
commercial license is granted per company and per project, in writing, and it does
not transfer ownership. This document is not a standing offer of a free commercial
license: nothing outside a written agreement from the copyright holder grants one.

What it covers: the code and documents in this repository only. The trained
weights, the corpora, the name and the private React interface are separate assets
with their own terms.

